RaceDay Non-Functional Requirements

1. Introduction

Non-functional requirements describe the qualities and performance characteristics that the RaceDay system should provide.

These requirements will guide development during the later stages of the project.



2. Security

NFR01 — Authentication

User accounts and protected functionality should require authentication.

NFR02 — Authorisation

The system should use role-based access control to restrict functionality.

NFR03 — Data Protection

User and participant information should be protected from unauthorised access.



3. Performance

NFR04 — Response Time

The API should provide responses within a reasonable amount of time under normal operating conditions.

NFR05 — Database Performance

Database queries should be designed efficiently to support normal system operations.



4. Usability

NFR06 — Ease of Use

The system should be straightforward for both Organisers and Participants to use.

NFR07 — Clear Information

Event, category, enrolment and result information should be presented clearly.

NFR08 — API Documentation

The API should be documented using Swagger/OpenAPI to assist with testing and development.



5. Reliability

NFR09 — Data Integrity

The database should maintain relationships and constraints to reduce invalid or inconsistent data.

NFR10 — Error Handling

The application should provide appropriate responses when errors occur.



6. Maintainability

NFR11 — Code Organisation

The application should use a clear and maintainable project structure.

NFR12 — Version Control

The project should use GitHub to track changes throughout development.

NFR13 — Continuous Integration

GitHub Actions should be used to automatically check the project when changes are committed.



7. Compatibility

NFR14 — Web Compatibility

The system should be designed to operate through modern web browsers.

NFR15 — Development Compatibility

The application should be developed using technologies compatible with .NET 8.



8. Scalability

NFR16 — Future Expansion

The system should be designed so that additional functionality can be added as the project develops.

Possible future functionality includes online payments, notifications, live tracking and mobile support.



9. Part 2

These non-functional requirements describe the intended quality characteristics of the RaceDay system.

Implementation and further refinement of these requirements will take place during Part 2.
